ce Prospero\"; should emerge as separate \"Red Death\" character\n   133→   - Modified: src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py\n   134→\n   135→## Key Insight for Fix Phase\n   136→\n   137→**The prompt-based approach is not working.** Three attempts have tried to fix this via LLM prompt improvements:\n   138→1. Attempt 1: Cross-group epithet resolution\n   139→2. Attempt 2: Proper name with article classification (caused the regression)\n   140→3. Attempt 3: Enhanced conflict detection prompts (did not work)\n   141→\n   142→**New approach needed:** Instead of relying on LLM judgment, implement a **structural/heuristic check**:\n   143→\n   144→1. **Pre-filter approach:** Before sending epithet-to-proper-name pairs to LLM, check if the epithet appears in sentences that describe CONFRONTATION with the proper name:\n   145→   - Look for verbs like: \"pursued\", \"confronted\", \"seized\", \"approached\", \"retreating from\"\n   146→   - If the epithet is the OBJECT of such verbs where the proper name is the SUBJECT, they are likely different entities\n   147→\n   148→2. **Example for this text:**\n   149→   - \"Prince Prospero... rushed hurriedly through the six chambers\" + \"the retreating figure\"\n   150→   - \"seizing the mummer\" (revellers seize the mummer)\n   151→   - \"Prince Prospero... had approached... to within three or four feet of the retreating figure\"\n   152→   - These patterns show the mummer/figure is being ACTED UPON separately from Prospero\n   153→\n   154→3. **Implementation location:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` in `_candidate_pairs_for_merge()` or early in `_llm_cross_group_resolution()`\n   155→\n   156→4. **Pseudo-code:**\n   157→   ```python\n   158→   def _entities_in_confrontation(entity1: str, entity2: str, text: str) -> bool:\n   159→       \"\"\"Check if two entities appear in confrontational relationship.\"\"\"\n   160→       confrontation_verbs = ['pursued', 'confronted', 'seized', 'attacked',\n   161→                             'approached', 'retreating', 'chased', 'fled']\n   162→       # Find sentences containing both entities\n   163→       # Check if one entity is agent and other is patient of confrontation verb\n   164→       # Return True if they appear to be opposing entities\n   165→   ```\n   166→\n   167→## Output Files\n   168→- HTML: output/masque_of_red_death/report.html\n   169→- JSON: output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json\n   170→\n   171→## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 4)\n   172→- Analysis completed successfully in ~7m\n   173→- 1 character detected: \"the Prince Prospero\" (alias: \"the mummer\")\n   174→- 1 character profile generated\n   175→- 73 pronunciation flags\n   176→- Character extraction time: 4m 28s (62.5% of total time)\n   177→- Note: LLM identity detection failed (server error 500)\n   178→- Note: Moral valence classification failed (server error 500)\n   179→\n   180→## Next Action\n   181→Re-run analysis with PROMPT_analyze.md to verify the confrontation detection fix resolves the \"the mummer\" / \"Prince Prospero\" merge issue.\n   182→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d9c3a4a-67c8-4785-8716-669c09fd45e6","uuid":"fa6f6a8e-26fa-4188-8b51-cfa53e8be5f0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"# Current Evaluation State\n\n## Active Text\n- **Name:** masque_of_red_death\n- **Attempt:** 5\n- **Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n- **baseline_score:** 6.75\n\n## Latest Scores\n- Structure Detection: 10/10\n- Character Extraction: 3/10 ← CRITICAL (unchanged from attempt 3)\n- Character Profiles: 5/10\n